# Trivy misconfiguration findings accepted on purpose, with the reason. Reviewed 2026-11-18.

# S3 and ECR use AWS-managed encryption (SSE-S3, AES256) rather than a customer-managed KMS
# key. The data is a public dataset (OULAD); a KMS key adds a monthly cost and key policy
# to manage for no gain here. A university deployment with real student data would use one.
AWS-0132
AWS-0033

# CloudWatch log groups are encrypted at rest by default with an AWS-managed key. The logs
# hold no request bodies (see infra/service/main.tf).
AWS-0017

# S3 server access logging needs a third bucket. Who did what is already in CloudTrail,
# which every AWS account has for management events.
AWS-0089

# X-Ray tracing is not needed for one function with one route that does the work.
AWS-0066
